<title>USA: VEBA's Phenolchemie plans Alabama plant.</title>
<headline>VEBA's Phenolchemie plans Alabama plant.</headline>
<dateline>MOBILE, Ala. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>VEBA AG's Phenolchemie plans to build a $150 million phenol/acetone plant here, the Mobile Area Chamber of Commerce said.</p>
<p>Initially, it said, the plant will produce 200,000 tonnes per year. The facility is slated to expand to 400,000 tonnes per year based on a projected increase in demand.</p>
<p>Construction is expected to begin early in 1998 on 30 acres adjacent to a facility operated by Huls America, another VEBA subsidiary.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
